course: dictionary
lesson: 1007
title: Bomb: one word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A bomb is a weapon that explodes to destroy things or hurt people. This is its main meaning, and it is a serious one. Be careful with the word in real life: «Jokes about bombs or weapons at an airport are treated as real threats.»
explain: The word also has friendlier meanings. A «bath bomb» is a fizzy ball you drop in the bath. Cost a bomb means cost a lot of money. When a film bombed, it failed badly. Look at the words around the word to choose the right meaning: is it a bath, a shop, a war, or a film?
explain: Some meanings are used only in certain places. In the UK, «cost a bomb» is a common phrase. A «bomb» dive is a jump into water with your knees hugged to your chest. The clues in the sentence tell you which meaning the writer means.
fact: A bomb is a weapon that explodes to destroy things or hurt people.
fact: To bomb means to attack with bombs.
fact: Informally, «to bomb» can mean to fail badly, as in «a film bombed».
fact: In the UK, «cost a bomb» means cost a lot of money.
fact: If you ever find a strange object or an old bomb, do not touch it. Move away and tell an adult or the police.
exercise: «Jokes about bombs or weapons at an airport are treated as real threats.» What does «threats» mean here? | Games for children | *Things that could cause harm | Tickets for a plane | Gifts from friends
exercise: «Her new film bombed at the cinema, and few people bought tickets.» What does «bombed» mean here? | Won lots of prizes | Exploded with a loud noise | *Failed badly | Was made in a bath
exercise: A bath bomb is a fizzy ball you drop in a bath. What does a bath bomb do? | It freezes the water solid | It makes the bath go dark | *It fizzes in the water | It is used to dive into the pool
test: Dad says the new car cost a bomb. What does he mean? | It was painted red | *It cost a lot of money | It was very small and light | It exploded in the garage
test: You find a strange object in the park that might be an old bomb. What should you do? | Pick it up to take it home | *Move away and tell an adult or the police | Kick it into the pond | Shout to your friends to come and look
exam: In «Jokes about bombs at an airport are treated as real threats», what does «treated» mean? | Ignored and forgotten | Cooked or baked | *Dealt with as if they are real and serious | Given away as a present
